# Review package: batch 2, slice delta

## 4cf35d39 Sweep every row and every socket route before sign-in

The sweep took one id per table, so it never asked about Zebra Payments, Maria or a
sub-unit, and a plain GET on a socket route is answered 404 by the socket plugin, so
an ungated terminal would have passed unseen. Now it takes every id (and checks the
sub-unit is among them), seeds a team under Zebra Payments and asks a department and
that team as a real pair. Socket routes are recorded and each is opened with injectWS
without a session, locally and over the link; it must be refused before anything is sent.

Seen failing first: a copy of the app with a route leaking a department name, and one
with an ungated socket route, each turned the test red. No production code changed.

Ruling: onRoute's type in app.ts left as is; the test types its callback wider - why: a function taking an optional websocket field is assignable, so no production change - cost if wrong: none

